  "conclusion": [
    "Neither frontend interaction recovers an exact VCR body. All168 previously exact functions remain exact.",
    "The syntax conversion uses added ordinary lexical scopes and separates for-loop declarations from their initializers without moving expressions. Compiling that same converted input as C++ preserves all180 raw bodies and relocation records plus25 typed objects and11 fields exactly, independently isolating the frontend effect.",
    "Under C, only the already-unmatched VCL,VCH,VCR bodies change. Both controls additionally emit all31 four-byte AMP b constants absent from the C++ object. Equal VCR span in the unsigned-arm C control is not a function match.",
    "Original readonly storage contains13 coefficient blocks and14 dewindow tables; the identified RSP group has dewindow without the coefficient block. The unchanged AMP header reproduces this asymmetry under C++, supporting the existing RSP language attribution jointly with Rich counts and grouping. This remains source-structure inference, not unique proof of original language.",
    "Canonical RSP source remains C++; the two diagnostic narrowed VCR bodies were not promoted."
  ],
